  evolved from: "Yes, the waggle dance is a remarkable example of how bees communicate the location of food sources. When a forager bee returns to the hive, it performs a waggle dance that encodes the direction and distance of the food. The angle of the waggle phase indicates the direction relative to the sun, while the duration signifies the distance. This intricate dance is a testament to the advanced communication methods in the animal kingdom."
